+- **Object store slow/down**
+  - What happens: segment uploads and bootstrap downloads stall; queries remain unaffected because shards serve from local disk.
+  - Detect: upload queue depth, manifest lag, local disk headroom.
+  - Recover: keep serving; throttle ingest when local disk watermark is hit; resume uploads when the store recovers.
 
-- **10x scale:** move to **hierarchical routing** (two-tier routers), enforce tenant isolation by default, and add SSD-friendly caching of rerank vectors (vector “hotset”).
-- **100x scale:** redesign storage into **tiered vector formats** (PQ-only cold tier, float16 warm, float32 hot), add **learned partitioning** (coarse quantizer routing) to reduce shard fanout, and make compaction globally scheduled (cluster-aware) to avoid synchronized IO storms.
